IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei3-part4-rulings-appeals`

-- Tests of ei3-part4-rulings-appeals.l4 (Act ss 90 to 94).
-- Expected values are hand-worked from the text of the section named beside each assertion. Every date is invented.

§ `s 90(1) who may ask what`

-- The nine questions of (a) to (i) are specified; the tenth constructor is "not on the list".
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 whether an employment is insurable`
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 how long an insurable employment lasts, including the dates on which it begins and ends`
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 what is the amount of any insurable earnings`
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 how many hours an insured person has had in insurable employment`
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 whether a premium is payable`
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 what is the amount of a premium payable`
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 who is the employer of an insured person`
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 whether employers are associated employers`
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 what amount shall be refunded under subsections 96(4) to (10)`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90(1) the question is one specified in section 90` `ei3 a question not named in subsection 90(1)`)
-- The five who may ask: an employer, an employee, a person claiming to be either, the Commission.
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the person may request a ruling of an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency on the question` `ei3 an employer` `ei3 whether an employment is insurable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the person may request a ruling of an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency on the question` `ei3 an employee` `ei3 how many hours an insured person has had in insurable employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the person may request a ruling of an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency on the question` `ei3 a person claiming to be an employer` `ei3 who is the employer of an insured person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the person may request a ruling of an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency on the question` `ei3 a person claiming to be an employee` `ei3 what is the amount of any insurable earnings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the person may request a ruling of an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency on the question` `ei3 the Commission` `ei3 whether a premium is payable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Someone not named, or a question not on the list: the subsection says nothing (not covered).
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the person may request a ruling of an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency on the question` `ei3 someone not named in subsection 90(1)` `ei3 whether an employment is insurable` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 90(1) the person may request a ruling of an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency on the question` `ei3 an employee` `ei3 a question not named in subsection 90(1)` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 90(2) to (4) time, reasonable time, presumption`

-- (2) The Commission at any time; others before the June 30 following the year to which the question relates (year 2025: before 30 June 2026).
#ASSERT `s 90(2) the request for a ruling is made in time` TRUE 2025 (YMD 2040 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 90(2) the request for a ruling is made in time` FALSE 2025 (YMD 2026 6 29)
#ASSERT `s 90(2) the request for a ruling is made in time` FALSE 2025 (YMD 2025 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90(2) the request for a ruling is made in time` FALSE 2025 (YMD 2026 6 30))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90(2) the request for a ruling is made in time` FALSE 2025 (YMD 2026 7 1))
-- (3)
#ASSERT `s 90(3) the authorized officer has made the ruling within a reasonable time` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90(3) the authorized officer has made the ruling within a reasonable time` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90(3) the authorized officer has made the ruling within a reasonable time` FALSE TRUE)
-- (4) "Unless a ruling has been requested": the deemings (a) and (b) hold only when none was.
#ASSERT `s 90(4)(a) the amount is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with this Act` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90(4)(a) the amount is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with this Act` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90(4)(a) the amount is deemed to have been deducted or paid in accordance with this Act` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 90(4)(b) the amount is deemed not to have been required to be deducted or paid in accordance with this Act` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90(4)(b) the amount is deemed not to have been required to be deducted or paid in accordance with this Act` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90(4)(b) the amount is deemed not to have been required to be deducted or paid in accordance with this Act` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 90.1: a ruling is required when a section 90 question arises in the consideration of a claim for benefits.
#ASSERT `s 90.1 a ruling must be made by an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` `ei3 whether an employment is insurable` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90.1 a ruling must be made by an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` `ei3 whether an employment is insurable` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90.1 a ruling must be made by an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` `ei3 a question not named in subsection 90(1)` TRUE)

§ `ss 91 to 94 appeals`

-- s 91: the Commission at any time; another person concerned within 90 days after being notified. Notified 3 March 2026: 3 March to
-- 31 March is 28 days, to 30 April 58, to 31 May 89, so the 90th day after is 1 June 2026 and that day counts.
-- (Correction: I first wrote the expected value here as 31 May, by hand; the rule gave 1 June, and a recount, confirmed with Python's
-- datetime, showed the rule was right. The expectation was changed, the rule was not.)
#ASSERT `s 91 the appeal to the Minister from the ruling is made in time` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 3) (YMD 2030 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 91 the appeal to the Minister from the ruling is made in time` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 3) (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 the appeal to the Minister from the ruling is made in time` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 3) (YMD 2026 6 2))
-- Notified 1 March 2026: the 90th day after is 30 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 91 the appeal to the Minister from the ruling is made in time` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 5 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 the appeal to the Minister from the ruling is made in time` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 5 31))
-- Someone not concerned and not the Commission cannot appeal, in time or not.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 the appeal to the Minister from the ruling is made in time` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2))
-- s 92: assessed on 10 January 2026 notice; 90 days after is 10 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 92 the employer may appeal to the Minister for a reconsideration of the assessment` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 4 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 92 the employer may appeal to the Minister for a reconsideration of the assessment` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 4 11))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 92 the employer may appeal to the Minister for a reconsideration of the assessment` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 11))
-- s 93(1): anyone who may be affected, and the Commission on an appeal of a ruling, is to be notified and heard.
#ASSERT `s 93(1) the person is to be notified of the Minister's intention to decide the appeal and heard` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 93(1) the person is to be notified of the Minister's intention to decide the appeal and heard` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(1) the person is to be notified of the Minister's intention to decide the appeal and heard` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 93(1) the Minister has done what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93(1) the Minister has done what the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(1) the Minister has done what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(1) the Minister has done what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 93(2) to (4)
#ASSERT `s 93(2) the appeal has been sent as required` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(2) the appeal has been sent as required` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(2) the appeal has been sent as required` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 93(3) the Minister has decided the appeal and notified the affected persons as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(3) the Minister has decided the appeal and notified the affected persons as required` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(3) the Minister has decided the appeal and notified the affected persons as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(3) the Minister has decided the appeal and notified the affected persons as required` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 93(4) the Minister may have the person notified in that manner` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(4) the Minister may have the person notified in that manner` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93(4) the Minister may have the person notified in that manner` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 94
#ASSERT `s 94 sections 90 to 93 restrict the Minister's authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94 sections 90 to 93 restrict the Minister's authority` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
